Changelog: 21-10-2026 14:25:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 13:23:31

Added. Xenia Manager: Xbox 360 games on the BC-250 with Xenia. Xenia has no stable releases, so the app pins one Xenia
Canary build, e6cd2e4 (20-10-2026), the Linux AppImage of its GitHub release, checked against its SHA-256, and says
when a build was published after it. The window says that Xenia's Linux build is experimental. It finds the games in
the chosen folders (Xbox 360 disc images, told by the disc's mark where Xenia looks for it; .xex files with their title
ID, an unpacked disc's default.xex under its folder's name; .zar archives; Games on Demand and Arcade packages under
the name in their header) and puts the ticked ones in Steam for Game Mode, "[X360] Title", the artwork drawn from the
app's icon. The Game Mode shortcuts run ~/.local/bin/bc250-xenia-run, which starts Xenia full screen
(--fullscreen=true); when Steam starts a game, a real controller is read instead of Steam's virtual one. Not tried on
the board yet: any game, the controllers under Steam Input.
